{#
    A self-dismissing toast for feedback inside a turbo-frame-scoped
    action (e.g. deleting a card from a list without a full-page
    navigation) - base.html.twig's own flash block only reads the
    success/error/info buckets, so a frame_toast-bucket message never
    gets rendered (and discarded) there first, and survives being read
    from deep inside a frame's own content instead.

    Bottom-anchored (the practice-round correct/incorrect toast keeps the
    top position - different role, gameplay feedback vs. a quiet
    confirmation) and solid neutral/neutral-content rather than a
    translucent primary tint - a low-opacity primary wash was reasonably
    visible in the light theme but nearly invisible in guitorial-dark
    (--color-primary there is a muted gold that barely lifts off a dark
    background at 10% opacity). neutral/neutral-content is DaisyUI's own
    always-high-contrast pairing, defined per theme specifically so a
    solid chip like this reads clearly regardless of which of the 4
    themes is active.
#}
{% for message in app.flashes('frame_toast') %}
    <div
            class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-4 z-50 flex justify-center pointer-events-none px-4"
            data-controller="toast"
    >
        <div class="animate-[toast-in-bottom_0.25s_ease-out] flex items-center gap-2 rounded-box bg-neutral px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-neutral-content shadow-xl">
            {{ message|trans }}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endfor %}
